SCOPE OF THIS LICENCE
---------------------

The MIT Licence below covers the contents of this repository only: the source code, the
documentation, and the public 5-minute ground truth in evaluation/gt/.

It does NOT cover the match data — the videos, the tracking data, the Smart Tagging and the
homography. Those assets are separately licensed for this competition only, under the terms you
accept at enrolment, and nothing in the licence below grants any right to use or redistribute
them. See DATA.md and RULES.md.

THE TWO WEIGHTS FILES AND THEIR TRAINING DATA
---------------------------------------------

The engine loads two weights files that the team trained offline:
engine/models/learned_v7.npz (the network) and engine/models/learned_pf_v7.npz (the per-frame
model). The MIT Licence below covers these two files as contents of this repository. It grants no
right in the datasets they were trained on. Those datasets stay under their own terms, and this
repository does not hold them. We credit them here:

- Sportec Open DFL: Bassek, M. et al. (2025), Scientific Data 12, 195,
  DOI 10.6084/m9.figshare.28196177. Licensed under CC BY 4.0.
- Metrica Sports sample data, github.com/metrica-sports/sample-data. Credited as its README asks.
- SkillCorner Open Data, github.com/SkillCorner/opendata. MIT licence, (c) 2020 SkillCorner.

PFF FC (now Gradient Sports) FIFA World Cup 2022 data was used as test data only, with credit to
PFF FC. No PFF match trained either weights file, and this repository holds no PFF data.

